  "question": {
    "text": "The dipole moment of a circular loop carrying a current <span style=\"font-family:georgia,serif;\">I</span>, is m and the magnetic field at the centre of the loop is <math><msub><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> . When the dipole moment is doubled by keeping the current constant, the magnetic field at the centre of the loop is <math><msub><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi>&#160;</mi></math> . The ratio&nbsp;<math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math> is:"
